This package includes RTKLIB, built into the extension for the post-processing of GNSS
observations (ppk_solve) and, from 0.8, for the conversion of raw receiver logs into RINEX
(raw_to_rinex, what RTKLIB's convbin does):

  RTKLIB-EX v2.5.1 (https://github.com/rtklibexplorer/RTKLIB, tag v2.5.1,
  commit 62d4677ed8425a4e2748c6d390b500d1afb493fc), sources in vendor/rtklib/src, unchanged.

  Of its receiver decoders (vendor/rtklib/src/rcv):
    ublox.c    u-blox,  Copyright (C) 2007-2020 by T. Takasu; Copyright (C) 2014 by T. Suzuki
    novatel.c  NovAtel, Copyright (C) 2007-2020 by T. Takasu
  Their headers carry these copyright lines ("All rights reserved") and name no licence: that they
  are under RTKLIB's BSD 2-clause licence below is inferred from the distribution (T. Takasu is the
  copyright holder of its license.txt), not stated in the files.

Not part of this package: RTKLIB's other receiver decoders (among them Septentrio, septentrio.c by
F. Tappero and J. Reimann; Trimble RT-17, rt17.c by D. A. Cook; Unicore, unicore.c by A. Malla: their
files name no licence of their own), streams and applications, and the routines of the IAU SOFA
library that RTKLIB bundles in sofa.c for the positions of the Sun and the Moon (an option that is
not built; SOFA has a licence of its own). See vendor/rtklib/VERSION.

